@startuml emergency-stop
!include ../_includes/theme.puml

title Emergency stop: keeper estop over curator session estop

actor "Operator" as P $PERSON
participant "keeper estop\n(the person's front)" as KE $SERVICE
participant "Session host\n(curator session estop)" as H $SERVICE
participant "task-board kernel\n(task-board's own code,\nno model)" as K $SERVICE
participant "Orchestrator sessions" as S $AGENT
participant "Runs" as R $AGENT
database "Boards" as B $COMMITTED

P -> KE: keeper estop [<hive>]
KE -> P: lists every session and run it will stop;\nasks for "EMERGENCY STOP" and presence
P -> KE: EMERGENCY STOP, with presence\n(OS user authentication or the companion app)
note right of KE
  the main loop may call it only under
  a delegation that names the trigger;
  every other agent session is refused
end note
KE -> H: estop [<process>]
H -> K: task-board board snapshot, per affected board
K -> B: runs in flight, Change Requests awaiting\nreview or integration, obligations, unrouted notices
H -> S: interrupt: write a short note (10-30 s, default 20)
S -> B: optional short note
H -> R: stop in a resumable way (open question)
H -> S: resumable stop (goals are kept)
H -> K: goal revision per board
K -> B: handoff_ref = snapshot + note
H -> KE: stopped, not stopped
KE -> P: report

== Later ==
P -> H: keeper up
H -> S: resume with the goal and its handoff note

caption Sources: spec §9, §11, §12.1; main-loop specification §10.3
@enduml
